	// zappy at full scale, in d phrygian. 30 bars, 65.15 s, five tempos.
	// the same piece as zappy-big-minor, bar for bar, drum for drum and
	// tempo for tempo, in the other key: its plan is that file's. this
	// one says only what differs.
	//
	// the key is d with its second note lowered, e flat, the half step
	// above home that glass-hour leans on. three things follow from it.
	// the chord beside home is e flat, a half step up, where the minor
	// one has b flat and c from below: dm dm eb dm (5-8), dm cm eb eb
	// (9-12), d eb d eb cm cm eb eb (13-20), cm eb d d cm eb d d (23-30).
	// the chord before each return home has an a in it against the e
	// flat, the interval that does not settle (bars 12, 19, 20). and the
	// motif's third note bends: a d e flat a | f, not a d e a | f. in the
	// return the motif is a d e flat a | f#: the bent note and the bright
	// last note together.
	//
	// bars 1 to 4 and the break (21, 22) are the ident unchanged, e
	// natural and all, in both pieces.
	//
	// what differs for the ear: the minor one climbs home from below and
	// arrives; this one grinds against the note next to home and falls
	// onto it. the minor is the brighter of the two.
